        "text": "Reads: 0:00-0:25 \"When an agent needs a human answer that has no API — it dials, it verifies, it returns what actually happened.\" 0:25-0:50 \"The bridge sits between an intent and a phone call. There are two trust lines: capability is not authority. Authority is not success.\" 0:50-1:20 \"Run it. Deny it. No call is placed. Grant it. A real call reaches a real number.\" 1:20-1:50 \"On Linux (Steam Deck), the same tool ran end-to-end. In the recovery workspace, two documented bugs were caught and fixed.\" 1:50-2:10 \"The hackathon asked: can code do phone work? Yes — provided you give it explicit authority, verify both directions, and log everything.\" Narration: Piper TTS (offline). No external services.",
